## 2. M6R-1 at the graduation: a deposit between migrate_v2 and the transition

The attacker sends [migrate_v2, deposit k x the new pool, crank_price] (the transition reads the inflated
lp_supply as its anchor: L_slow = min(the curve's L_slow, anchor)), then withdraws.  As built L_slow keeps the
curve's value, ~1.35x the pool's depth, and decays at tau_slow = 1 h; with M6R-1 the first PumpSwap observation
caps it at the pool's locked depth D (the burned creation LP).  Cells: L_slow / sqrt(X*(Y + VQR)) at the
transition second, 1 s, 9 s (the gate), 900 s and 3600 s after it; the cap q/X of an open 900 s after the
transition (the boost window; the boost is spent by then).

| market | move | rule | L_slow / depth at +0 / +1 / +9 / +900 / +3600 s | open cap q/X at +900 s |
