## 3. M6R-1 in steady state on a PumpSwap pool (market C: the fresh graduate after its boost, Tier C)

(a) A deposit of k x the pool held for H and pulled in the second a genuine 3x/120 s pump starts (the keeper on
its coverage duties, #101 keeper).  L_ema and L_slow follow the deeper pool while it is held; the exit reference
L_b = max(L_live, min(max(L_ema', L_slow), cap)) then credits the pulled depth unless the cap floor(D*1e4/
lambda_min) binds.  Cells: the exit (seconds after the pump starts, price); L_b / the pool's depth at the pump's
first second.

| deposit | held | M6 as built (#104) | #105 |
|---|---|---|---|
| none | 600 s | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 1.00 | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 1.00 |
| 1x the pool | 600 s | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 2.00 | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 2.00 |
| 1x the pool | 3600 s | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 2.00 | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 2.00 |
| 3x the pool | 600 s | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 3.99 | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 2.00 |
| 3x the pool | 3600 s | open; L_b/depth 4.00 | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 2.00 |
| 7x the pool | 3600 s | open; L_b/depth 8.00 | liquidation +73 s @2.22x; L_b/depth 2.00 |

(b), (c) An open at the cap after the deposit was held for H (still in during the open), or wrapped around the
open alone; every third-party LP unit then leaves.  Cells: the position's q / X of the pool after the
withdrawal (the honest open: 1x); a deposit wrapped around the open inflates nothing (the minimum drops X_now,
and L_slow, D and the ring's EMA state do not move within the transaction), a held one pushes L_slow, which
the D term bounds at lambda/lambda_min of the burned LP's depth:

