| 3x the pool | held 3600 s | 7.087 % (2.87x) | 4.939 % (2.00x) |
| 7x the pool | held 3600 s | 13.137 % (5.32x) | 4.939 % (2.00x) |
| 3x the pool | held 14400 s | 9.737 % (3.94x) | 4.939 % (2.00x) |
| 7x the pool | held 14400 s | 19.422 % (7.86x) | 4.939 % (2.00x) |

(d) FITS-2 on PumpSwap: C's pool with as much third-party LP again (lambda 50 %), which the attacker holds; a
position at a fraction of the cap; flat 30 s, then a genuine pump to a hold level just below the honest
threshold (healthy at the pool's depth).  From its first second the attacker sends [withdraw all, crank_price,
deposit] (the withdraw drag: its attacker-only seconds pull L_ema to D) and [withdraw all, liquidate, deposit]
every second.  The liquidation spot leg at L_live (#100) or at max(L_live, L_ema') (FITS-2 (a), #101), each
with the #99 keeper (per second only near a threshold, else every 30 s) or the #101 keeper (FITS-2 (b): per
second for 10 s after a foreign bucket liquidity, extended while it recurs); every column with #105's D rules.
Cells: the attacked outcome at each hold level (the honest keeper leaves every one of them open):

