(e) M6D-1: (b)'s held deposit sizes the open, then leaves at a genuine pump.  An LP deposits k x the pool
and holds it 1 h (a crank every 30 s); a position of `size` x the cap is opened on the deepened pool (sized
on the held deposit: X0's D term allows lambda/lambda_min of the burned LP's depth, 2x at lambda_min 50 %);
in the next second a genuine pump to top x over 120 s starts and the LP withdraws every third-party unit in
its first second (or keeps it: the control).  L_slow (tau 1 h) still credits the deposit, so the reference
L_b stays at the cap floor(D*1e4/lambda_min) while the pool is back at D; the #101 keeper tries every
covered second.  Cells: the exit (seconds after the pump starts, price); q / the honest cap; the lenders'
P&L against Q's value at the exit's spot; the borrower's share of V.

